  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "When declaring an UdonSharpBehaviour variable (in mainline, official UdonSharp), it usually doesn't work right out of the box and when saved, the Unity console explanation for why it cannot compile says: \"Cannot find UdonSharpBehaviour Are you missing a reference\". This is extremely misleading and also factually incorrect. It makes it look like you cannot have an UdonSharpBehavior as a variable (which you 100% can). This is actually a pretty serious issue because it can lead to users assuming that you simply cannot actually use the broader 'UdonSharpBehaviour' type as a variable at all, and may encourage extremely complex and low-performance antipatterns to circumvent needing to use it.\n\nThe issue is also inconsistent, since sometimes removing the Tooltip decorator after letting Unity see that indeed it can compile an UdonSharpBehaviour with an UdonSharpBehaviour variable in it, it will work just fine.",
